I have received the chain letter you mentioned at least ten times during
the time I've been on Usenet.  I don't find it very amusing.  The
subject matter is irrelevant.

I am tying up my equipment and phone lines while downloading this
garbage.  I am fortunate in the respect that I do not have to pay by the
byte for news or mail.  Many people do.  If you had to pay the cost of
postage for every silly piece of junk snail-mail you receive, would you
not be angered by receiving it?

